 * ``(4, 2, 0, "beta", 1)`` → "4.2 beta 1"
+
+Starting with Django 2028, the ``VERSION`` tuple has four elements, as
+calendar versions have no minor version:
+
+#. Year.
+#. Patch number, 0 for the feature release.
+#. Status -- can be one of "alpha", "beta", "rc" or "final".
+#. Series number, as above.
+
+A patch number of 0 is never shown in the version. Some examples:
+
+* ``(2028, 0, "alpha", 0)`` → "2028 pre-alpha"
+
+* ``(2028, 0, "beta", 1)`` → "2028 beta 1"
+
+* ``(2028, 0, "final", 0)`` → "2028"
+
+* ``(2028, 1, "final", 0)`` → "2028.1"
